       query-rx-filter  (Command) Return rx-filter information for all NICs (or for the given NIC).

       Arguments:

       "name: string" (optional)
           net client name

       Returns: list of "RxFilterInfo" for all NICs (or for the given NIC).  Returns an error if the given "name" doesn't exist, or given NIC doesn't support rx-filter querying, or
       given net client isn't a NIC.

       Since: 1.6

       Example:

               -> { "execute": "query-rx-filter", "arguments": { "name": "vnet0" } }
               <- { "return": [
                       {
                           "promiscuous": true,
                           "name": "vnet0",
                           "main-mac": "52:54:00:12:34:56",
                           "unicast": "normal",
                           "vlan": "normal",
                           "vlan-table": [
                               4,
                               0
                           ],
                           "unicast-table": [
                           ],
                           "multicast": "normal",
                           "multicast-overflow": false,
                           "unicast-overflow": false,
                           "multicast-table": [
                               "01:00:5e:00:00:01",
                               "33:33:00:00:00:01",
                               "33:33:ff:12:34:56"
                           ],
                           "broadcast-allowed": false
                       }
                     ]
                  }

